WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.348 --> 00:00:03.900
- So, first up, we have Michael B. Jordan,

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.804
in the boxing movie, Creed.

00:00:05.804 --> 00:00:07.799
- You know he's great, a great performer,

00:00:07.799 --> 00:00:09.679
great actor, great looking guy,

00:00:09.679 --> 00:00:11.791
my only question is, is he too young?

00:00:11.791 --> 00:00:12.608
- Exactly,

00:00:12.608 --> 00:00:13.688
I mean are we really gonna give

00:00:13.688 --> 00:00:15.488
such a grand achievement to somebody

00:00:15.488 --> 00:00:18.252
with such a modest body of work?

00:00:18.252 --> 00:00:21.384
- Oscar should go to someone
who's been tested, you know?

00:00:21.384 --> 00:00:23.732
Someone who's seasoned.

00:00:23.732 --> 00:00:24.544
Someone who's--

00:00:24.544 --> 00:00:25.138
- Jennifer Lawrence.

00:00:25.138 --> 00:00:26.056
- [All] Yes.

00:00:26.056 --> 00:00:26.881
- Yes yes yes.

00:00:26.881 --> 00:00:29.177
- I mean you look at her, and you think.

00:00:30.575 --> 00:00:34.409
Warmth, talent, safety.

00:00:34.409 --> 00:00:36.313
- Something that I
didn't feel from Jordan.

00:00:36.313 --> 00:00:37.472
- Especially safety.

00:00:37.472 --> 00:00:37.835
- Yeah.

00:00:37.835 --> 00:00:38.726
- My thoughts exactly.

00:00:38.726 --> 00:00:40.249
- So I think we're all in agreement,

00:00:40.249 --> 00:00:41.641
Jennifer Lawrence for best actress?

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.375
- Yes, absolutely.

00:00:43.375 --> 00:00:45.767
- Moving right along, we have uh,

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:48.507
Straight Out Of Comp-ton,
for best picture,

00:00:48.507 --> 00:00:50.271
am I saying that right? Comp-ton?

00:00:50.271 --> 00:00:53.560
- Wow, just an awe inspiring body of work.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:56.126
- I remember sitting there
in the theater thinking that,

00:00:56.126 --> 00:00:59.045
but, you know, it also
fell a little short for me.

00:00:59.045 --> 00:01:01.181
I just couldn't connect.

00:01:01.181 --> 00:01:03.630
Something just, it just
wasn't believable enough.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.979
- You know, I agree.

00:01:04.979 --> 00:01:06.360
I mean the point of a film like this

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.053
is to convey the poetry of a journey.

00:01:09.053 --> 00:01:11.260
- Well, if we're talking about journeys,

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:14.734
we may as well mention
Matt Daemon's journey.

00:01:14.734 --> 00:01:16.406
From Mars?

00:01:16.406 --> 00:01:17.417
- Yes.

00:01:17.417 --> 00:01:18.753
- Mars is so far!

00:01:18.753 --> 00:01:19.345
(giggling)

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.054
- I mean you drive from Comp-ton

00:01:21.054 --> 00:01:23.297
to Hollywood a couple
times in an afternoon,

00:01:23.297 --> 00:01:25.981
but try going from Comp-ton
to Mars more than once?

00:01:27.221 --> 00:01:30.380
- Can you imagine how many
potatoes you would need for that?

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:31.804
(laughter)

00:01:31.804 --> 00:01:34.276
That entire film just portrayed

00:01:34.276 --> 00:01:36.112
such a harsh environment,

00:01:36.112 --> 00:01:38.040
where the average person
would have fallen victim,

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:40.383
but he was able to overcome.

00:01:40.383 --> 00:01:40.651
- Yes.

00:01:40.651 --> 00:01:41.942
- You know Matt Daemon seems like

00:01:41.942 --> 00:01:43.324
someone you could just grab a beer with,

00:01:43.324 --> 00:01:45.726
you know, like a friend, or a colleague.

00:01:45.726 --> 00:01:46.965
- Or a husband.

00:01:48.618 --> 00:01:50.406
- Well, I think we're all in agreement,

00:01:50.406 --> 00:01:53.031
that we're nominating The
Martian for best picture.

00:01:53.031 --> 00:01:54.039
- Yes.

00:01:54.039 --> 00:01:55.874
- Okay, let's see, what else.

00:01:55.874 --> 00:01:57.563
Oh, of course.

00:01:57.563 --> 00:02:01.604
Beast of No Nation, actor Abraham, Atta?

00:02:01.604 --> 00:02:03.208
For the best leading role.

00:02:03.208 --> 00:02:04.971
- You know I loved him in The Wire,

00:02:04.971 --> 00:02:07.125
but this time around he just felt...

00:02:08.084 --> 00:02:09.074
A little bit...

00:02:11.079 --> 00:02:12.519
Incorrect.

00:02:12.519 --> 00:02:13.775
- Yeah.

00:02:13.775 --> 00:02:14.510
- Yeah.

00:02:21.478 --> 00:02:23.010
- I love these chocolate chip cookies,

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:26.922
but something just tastes
a little off about them.

00:02:26.922 --> 00:02:28.153
- They're too chocolatey right?

00:02:28.153 --> 00:02:29.349
- Too chocolatey.

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:31.137
- I try to eat around the chocolate chips.

00:02:31.137 --> 00:02:32.616
Pretend they're not even there.

